#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Instrument for navigation and time to preview, for one or more file managers on one fixture.

  flea-field-nav calibrate [--delays 0,50,200] [--runs 10]   the shared method on tests/search-calib.qml
  flea-field-nav selftest                                    detector and key table over recorded logs, no display
  flea-field-nav preflight                                   core needs ok/MISSING, each entrant named, exit 0
  flea-field-nav measure PLAN.json                           run a plan: see measure()'s docstring for its JSON
  flea-field-nav report JSONL                                median [min..max] tables and ratios to Strata
  flea-field-nav explore ENTRANT FIXTURE COLUMN [--kind K] [--view V] [--flea TREE] [--preview MODE] [--out DIR] [--json FILE]

Launch columns ride the same plan: launch.first_frame.<size> (exec to the first presented frame of the window), launch.first_rows.<size> (exec to the first frame whose content region shows INK_ROWS ink rows, default VISIBLE_ROWS 25) and launch.settled.<size> (the last change before 2 s of quiet, cap 15 s), off one full-output recorder run from exec with the bar masked.
Cold is prepared by the caller (page and thumbnail caches dropped before the run); the plan stamps "cache": "cold" or "warm" in the manifest so a number is never read without its cache state.
The method is tools/flea-field-search's: tools/flea-framecap stamps the frames that differ in a rectangle in CLOCK_MONOTONIC, and keys go to the ydotool socket stamped in CLOCK_MONOTONIC just before the write, so key and frame share one clock.
This tool imports that file (SourceFileLoader, no copy) and reuses its detector, input path, recorder, launch lines, regions and report maths.
Columns time the keystroke to the first frame in which the entrant's content region changes (first) and to the last change before 2 s of quiet, cap 15 s (settled).
The columns are nav.cursor.inview.<view> (one untimed Down, quiet, then 7 timed Downs at a 400 ms pace inside the first screen) and nav.cursor.scroll.<view> (Downs past the bottom edge, quiet, then 12 timed Downs that each scroll).
The columns go on with nav.enter.<view> and nav.back.<view> (one Down selects the folder, quiet, Enter into its 1000 entries, quiet, the back key out) and preview.<kind> (quicklook: Space on the file; pane: the Down that lands on it, watched in the right 40 percent of the content region, refined per entrant with explore).
The ql column times Quick Look on a 4096 byte Markdown document that opens with a 40-row table (ql_md_table_first) against a tableless one of the same size (ql_md_plain), each in a launch of its own so every sample is a first open, key to settled_ms; a byte-identical twin (ql_md_plain_b) is the negative control.
report prints INCOMPLETE with no twin rows, INVALID when the twin control reports INSTRUMENT-NOISE, else SHIP when p95(table) <= p95(plain) + the control's own gap |p95(plain) - p95(twin)|, else HOLD.
An entrant without the preview feature gets a "no feature" row, never a silent gap.
The NAV key table's copies live under .flea-local/ref/apps/ and are close to the installed versions; every chord is checked on the operator's box with explore before measuring, and a copy that differs is re-cited there.
The pane preview's stimulus is the cursor move that lands on the file: the last Down of the walk there, or an Up back to row 0 when the file is first.
Sample input, one recorder line: "F 660389861257350 660389874933379 32 95 126" (presentation ns, received ns, rows).
Sample plan: {"out": "o.jsonl", "runs": 5, "fixtures": {"nav500": "D/nav500"}, "arms": [{"id": "f", "entrant": "flea"}]}.
Sample row: {"arm": "f", "column": "nav.cursor.inview.list", "per_key_first_ms": [4.4, 4.7], "settled_ms": 40.1}.
"""
